From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:43:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] 2026-08-27 review: contact-rate evidence, service
 screening, objection colour

Frank walked the 08-27 rebuild and found errors in both directions. Each fix
below is one of them.

CONTACT RATE
* A no-contact note no longer vetoes the rest of the day. It was checked first
  and returned immediately, so Sarahi's 11:49 "Called No Answer" on Ricardo
  Perea outranked her own 13:25 note "Spoke with Ricardo have appoiment set for
  1:30" and the 15m44s recording behind it. A negative is now overruled by the
  producer explicitly stating contact, or by a sustained (>=60s) live
  recording. Jose Garcia and Guadalupe Garcia were lost the same way.
* Text in a notes field is no longer proof of a conversation. "Rachel Anderson"
  (a jotted name), a pasted coaching script and a to-do list all carried rows
  into the contact rate. Notes must now look like a report of the call; a
  stronger test gates the override above.
* Duration alone no longer promotes a dial to live. It was the only basis for
  Guillermo Lara and Cynthia Atondo, both of which Frank read as nobody
  answering, and nothing on the day was correctly promoted by it.
* A dial under 5s with no recording cannot be live -- Roger Ryan's 1-second
  second number was riding the other call's note.
* One row per lead: a lead reachable on two numbers was two contacts.
* "Hello? Robert?" and nothing else now classifies as No Answer, not live. The
  HUMAN pattern matched the producer's own greeting, and the strongest-verdict
  rank then let it beat a full "mailbox is full" greeting on the same number.

SERVICE / RENEWAL
* Inbound screening drops the CSR condition. Outbound needs it (Wesley
  Knowlton), but a customer calling IN with an open ticket and no open lead is
  calling about service whoever owns the ticket -- Armando Alvarez, whom
  Crystal transferred straight to a Spanish speaker, counted as a 455s contact.

DISPLAY
* Lost is read off the move DESTINATION, not the whole string. Jose Gonzalez
  moved "Dead to ... Quoted" -- out of Dead -- and printed as a lost lead while
  AgencyZoom still has him open at status 0.
* Objection chips carry two axes: texture for whether the producer engaged it,
  colour for whether the lead took a lost action (moved to dead, or
  smart-cycled more than 30 days out). Maria de Avina is mid-quote with a
  callback booked and was printing the same red as a dead lead.
* Call-in / call-back badges reuse the outcome chip's stripes and ink.

THROTTLE
* Recording downloads pace at 8/min and honour Retry-After. RingCentral's media
  endpoint allows 10 per rolling 60s; both call sites asked for 12, and on
  08-27 the window saturated and the run ground for 30 minutes at record 115 of
  203, which would have left 88 dials with no recording.

