From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:48:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Re-screen cached inbound calls at read time

The transcripts file is a cache, so a call already transcribed stayed in Call
Detail even once a later screening rule would have dropped it. Armando Alvarez
survived the inbound service rule written to exclude him purely because his
audio was already on disk from the previous run. Screening is pure record
logic and costs nothing, so it now runs at read time as well as before
download.

