From 46589af47c6113e2960e5759e4042494f56d237f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 05:46:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Call-in badge: stripe in the tint, ink in the dark

The badge striped at full paint saturation and coloured its text the same
paint, so the word sat on its own colour and vanished -- amber on amber
(Frank, 2026-08-28: "both emails were visually unreadable"). It also never
got its white base, because .badge-new is defined later in the sheet and its
`background` shorthand repainted the base solid green underneath the stripes.

Outlined categories already carry the right pair in digest_config -- `stripe`
for the wash and `ink` for the text -- so reuse them; filled categories have
no tint of their own, so _tint() mixes one into white. background-color is
now set inline alongside background-image so the later rule cannot win.

Caught only after it had gone out. A rendered screenshot of the Call Detail
panel belongs in the pre-send check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vnt6SJK5LgkQPDc7X6ThUW
---
